            <ArticleTitle>TREX1 dictates the immune fate of irradiated cancer cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1339857</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/2162402X.2017.1339857</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The optimal radiation dose and fractionation to induce anti-tumor immunity remain elusive. We recently found that the exonuclease TREX1 abrogates the immunogenicity of irradiated cancer cells by degrading interferon-stimulatory cytosolic dsDNA. TREX1 upregulation by radiation dose per fraction beyond a threshold of 10-12 Gy results in poor synergy with immune checkpoint blockers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
